WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:05.303
Place a short pre-curve in the last three
flutes of a size eight or ten hand file.

2
00:00:07.582 --> 00:00:11.570
In a tight canal, wall contact straightens
the pre-curve before it reaches the

3
00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:11.823
turn.

4
00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:15.596
The straightened tip stops at the curve.

5
00:00:15.742 --> 00:00:17.446
Record this as the available length.

6
00:00:18.531 --> 00:00:22.890
MicroPath, size fifteen or seventeen with a
point zero three taper, enlarges the

7
00:00:22.915 --> 00:00:24.093
approach above the curve.

8
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:26.186
This creates clearance for the short pre-
curve.

9
00:00:27.599 --> 00:00:31.052
Reintroduce the pre-curved size eight or ten
hand file.

10
00:00:31.311 --> 00:00:33.279
The short bend now has room to reach the
turn.

11
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.543
Continue watch winding: thirty degrees
clockwise, then thirty degrees

12
00:00:37.603 --> 00:00:38.427
counterclockwise.

13
00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:41.517
The shoulder contacts the wall while the
pre-curved tip enters the continuation.

14
00:00:44.536 --> 00:00:47.776
Feel the drop as the file advances beyond
the previous stop.

15
00:00:48.109 --> 00:00:51.456
Continue this winding motion as the file
follows the canal deeper.

16
00:00:52.514 --> 00:00:54.619
Consider the same mechanism in this tooth.

17
00:01:00.636 --> 00:01:04.192
The prepared approach gives the short pre-
curve room to reach the turn.

18
00:01:04.425 --> 00:01:07.442
Maintain watch winding as the instrument
adapts to the canal.
